=== PARITY (vs web ChargingTab.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (ChargingSummarySource -> ChargingTabModel):
    useTranslation, useFormatting (currency). The web component takes `data: FleetAnalytics` as a
    prop; the native model is fed coalesced snapshots by a source. The view performs NO HTTP. The
    embedded ChargingDetailSection owns its own ChargingDetailModel (web composes the same `data`).
  Projection -> ChargingTabProjection is a 1:1 port: safe(v)=finite?v:0 (web `safe`/`safeNumber`);
    the six summary cards map total_charging_sessions / total_energy_kwh / total_cost (always shown)
    and power_stats.avg / duration_stats.avg / efficiency_stats.avg (optional — `nil` reproduces the
    web `stats ? … : '—'`, where the em dash shows only when the whole StatsSummary is absent, NOT
    when avg==0); donut slice colors wrap at six (web `PIE_COLORS[i % PIE_COLORS.length]`); the hourly
    composed chart re-projects energy onto the charges domain + trailing axis (web `yAxisId=left`
    charges / `yAxisId=right` energy). All verified by EXECUTED XCTest (32/32).
  Composition (web order) -> 6 summary MetricCards (Sessions/Total Energy/Total Cost/Avg Power/Avg
    Duration/Charge Efficiency) -> Charger Types donut -> Start Battery Distribution bars -> Hourly
    Charging Pattern composed chart -> <ChargingDetailSection data={data}/>. CHART_COLORS parity:
    donut PIE_COLORS[0..5], battery bars [1], hourly charges [0] + energy [3].
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSChartPalette /
    TSChartFormat / tsGlassPanel / TSFadeIn / TSSkeleton / tsChartAxes compiled against the REAL
